cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "healpix-connector: connect existing data repositories to the HEALPix grid, with declared support, valid time and uncertainty"
abstract: >-
  A Python library that puts data from existing repositories onto the HEALPix
  discrete global grid as GRID4EARTH uses it (NESTED ordering on the WGS84
  ellipsoid), and states for every value the support it was measured over, the
  time it is valid for, and its uncertainty. Occurrence records are read from
  their repository on request, never mirrored, and are returned with the cells
  their positional uncertainty covers, the download DOI and the taxonomy used.
  Environmental sources are read as zarr-conventions/dggs datasets described by
  a STAC item; converters are provided for CHELSA climatologies, and Climate DT
  is read through GRID4EARTH's healpix-convert.
